# Linux Basic Commands

## ✅ 1. Navigation Commands

### pwd – Print Working Directory

Shows the current location in the filesystem.

pwd

📌 Output example:

![Image](../../Images/pwd.png)

### ls – List Directory Contents

Lists files and folders in the current directory.

ls

![alt text](../../Images/ls.png) [alt text](<Linux Basic Commands>)

->ls -l → Detailed list (permissions, size, date)
->ls -a → Shows hidden files (those starting with .)
->ls -la → Combined

### cd – Change Directory

Moves into a directory.

cd folder_name

Examples:

![alt text](../../Images/cd.png)

## ✅ 2. File and Directory Management

### mkdir – Make Directory

Creates a new folder.

mkdir new_folder

![alt text](../../Images/mkdir.png)

### touch – Create File

Creates an empty file.

touch file.txt

![alt text](../../Images/touch.png)

### cp – Copy Files or Directories

cp source.txt destination.txt

![alt text](../../Images/cp.png)

-> Copy folder:

cp -r folder1 folder2

### mv – Move or Rename Files

mv oldname.txt newname.txt

![alt text](../../Images/mv1.png)

mv file.txt ~/Documents/

![alt text](../../Images/mv2.png)

### rm – Remove Files

rm file.txt

![alt text](../../Images/rmfile.png)

rm -r folder_name

![alt text](../../Images/rmfolder.png)

⚠️ Be careful! There is no undo.

## ✅ 3. File Viewing & Editing

### cat – View File Contents

Displays content in terminal.

cat file.txt

![alt text](../../Images/cat.png)

### nano – Edit Files in Terminal

A basic terminal-based text editor.

nano file.txt


->Use arrows to move
->ctrl + o to save
->ctrl + x to exit

### clear – Clears the Terminal

clear

![alt text](../../Images/clear.png)

Shortcut: ctrl+l

## ✅ 4. System Commands

### echo – Print Text

Useful for debugging or scripting.

echo "Hello, World!"

![alt text](../../Images/echo.png)

### whoami – Show Current User

whoami

![alt text](../../Images/whoami.png)

### man – Manual for Any Command

man ls

Use q to quit manual.

## ✅ 5. Searching and Finding

find - Locate Files

find . -name "*.txt"

![alt text](../../Images/find.png)

🔍 Finds all .txt files in current folder and subfolders.

## ✅ 6. Helpful Shortcuts


| Shortcut   | Action                      |
| ---------- | --------------------------- |
| `Tab`      | Auto-complete files/folders |
| `↑ / ↓`    | Browse command history      |
| `CTRL + C` | Stop a running command      |
| `CTRL + L` | Clear screen                |

## ✅ 7. Bonus: Chaining Commands

-> Run multiple commands:

mkdir test && cd test && touch hello.txt

![alt text](../../Images/mkdir.png)

-> Run only if previous command succeeds: &&
-> Run regardless of success: ;